PICS 0
BACnet Protocol Implementation Conformance Statement
Vendor Name: "Chipkin Automation Systems"
Product Name: "CAS BACnet Stack Example - B-AEC"
Product Model Number: "CAS BACnet Stack Example - B-AEC"
Product Description: "A BACnet/IP advanced elevator controller built on the CAS BACnet Stack. It reports what an elevator installation (an Elevator Group, a Lift and an Escalator) is doing and accepts commands: WriteProperty and WritePropertyMultiple to three commandable outputs and to the Elevator Group's Landing_Call_Control (a landing call is served by a simulated lift car). It supports SubscribeCOV and SubscribeCOVPropertyMultiple, generates intrinsic event notifications (CHANGE_OF_STATE on the Lift's Passenger_Alarm), accepts AcknowledgeAlarm, answers GetEventInformation, keeps an Event Log (read with ReadRange), drives an output from a Schedule, accepts TimeSynchronization, DeviceCommunicationControl and ReinitializeDevice including backup and restore of its configuration, lets a client create and delete Analog Value objects, and is discoverable by Who-Is and Who-Has (it can also initiate a Who-Is). It is a tutorial for implementers of the B-AEC profile."

